      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If Continuous_Heart_Rate is missing because low-income patients systematically refuse to\n",
        "transmit telemetry due to mobile data costs, then the missingness is MNAR (Missing Not At Random).\n",
        "\n",
        "Why?\n",
        "The missingness is not random. It is driven by a meaningful underlying patient characteristic\n",
        "that is tied to the mechanism producing the missing data. This means the probability of being\n",
        "missing is related to a substantive factor linked to the data-generating process.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why not MCAR?\n",
        "Because the missingness is clearly systematic rather than random.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why mean imputation is harmful:\n",
        "Mean imputation would artificially reduce the variance of the heart-rate variable, distort the\n",
        "true distribution, weaken real relationships in the data, and erase the socioeconomic pattern\n",
        "embedded in the missingness. This would damage the integrity of the dataset and produce\n",
        "misleading inference."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MFWp6--V__y7"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Suppose Primary_Diagnosis_Code has 850 unique categories. A junior analyst uses pd.get_dummies()\n",
        "to create 850 binary dummy columns and also includes an intercept in the regression.\n",
        "\n",
        "For every observation:\n",
        "D1 + D2 + ... + D850 = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "But the intercept column is also a column of ones.\n",
        "\n",
        "So:\n",
        "Intercept = D1 + D2 + ... + D850\n",
        "\n",
        "This creates perfect multicollinearity. One column is an exact linear combination of the others.\n",
        "As a result, the design matrix X is not full rank, X'X becomes singular, and the OLS estimator\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_hat = (X'X)^(-1) X'y\n",
        "\n",
        "cannot be computed because (X'X)^(-1) does not exist.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is why including all dummy variables together with an intercept mathematically destroys\n",
        "the OLS estimator."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0QfEmbqnAEol"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "encoder = TargetEncoder(cols=['Primary_Diagnosis_Code'])\n",
